        "detail": "Six cable plugs (e-stop, start cord, two 6-pin SH motor/encoder plugs, Qwiic sensor, battery) sit on the left and right edges at 10 mm pitch, with USB-C at the bottom and the module's antenna keep-out at the top. Each side needs about 35 mm of edge length, with finger room to seat and pull cables, so the board cannot shrink to the 74x12 mm placement minimum. The 80x60 size also leaves room for the DRV8833 motor traces and the 2 A motor supply."
